In this study, we developed the CG-AMP model based on the PyTorch framework and conducted training on a Linux server equipped with an NVIDIA RTX 3090Ti GPU. The model was optimized using the Adam optimizer, with the learning rate set to 0.001. During training, a batch size of 32 and a total of 50 epochs were used. In addition, a validation set was employed to select effective model parameters, and the final performance was evaluated on an independent test set. The model was further fine-tuned using appropriate hyperparameters to achieve better performance. Key parameters are summarized in Table 3. In the binary classification task of distinguishing AMPs from non-AMPs, to ensure the comparability of our findings with existing literature, we use five common classification evaluation metrics: Accuracy (Acc), Recall (Rec), Precision (Pre), F1-score and Matthews Correlation Coefficient (MCC)46. The metrics are calculated as follows:15\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
